28. MANDATORY END-TO-END TEST SCENARIOS
==================================================

Test complete workflows using controlled test fixtures clearly separated from production data.

TEST A — RFQ ENABLED:

Company RFQ enabled.
Approved PR exists.
Future RFQ Floating retrieves the eligible PR.
RFQ is created.
Supplier invitations are issued.
Supplier quotations are received.
Examiner processes the quotations.
Technical and commercial evaluations complete.
Comparative statement is generated.
Award is approved.
Vendor Item Price Register is activated.
PO retrieves approved prices.
Vendor allocation is calculated.
Approver reviews and approves.
PO is released.

TEST B — RFQ DISABLED:

Company or branch RFQ disabled.
Valid Purchase Price Book exists.
PR is created.
PO retrieves the approved Price Book price.
Correct quantity tier and discount are applied.
PO is approved and released.

TEST C — MULTI-VENDOR ALLOCATION:

Two or more vendors are approved for one item.
Allocation totals 100%.
PO quantity is split correctly.
Price and allocation snapshots are preserved.
Buyer proposes a deviation.
Approver sees the original and proposed values.
Authorized decision is recorded.

TEST D — DUAL UOM:

PR uses Inventory UOM.
RFQ uses Purchase UOM.
Price Register uses Purchase UOM.
PO uses Purchase UOM.
Goods Receipt converts into Inventory UOM.
Inventory balance updates correctly.

TEST E — LOCAL LLM:

Download an eligible model.
Verify download.
Install compatible runtime.
Deploy model.
Run health check.
Set model as default.
Execute local RFQ examination.
Ask a question in Examiner Chat.
Verify evidence references.
Change default model.
Confirm task-specific selection.
Stop model.
Verify fallback behavior and error reporting.

TEST F — SECURITY:

Unauthorized user cannot access another company's RFQ.
Supplier cannot access competing quotations.
Technical evaluator cannot access sealed commercial information prematurely.
Unauthorized user cannot override allocation.
Chat cannot approve an RFQ.
Cloud examiner remains unavailable unless explicitly authorized.

TEST G — FAILURE AND RECOVERY:

Missing price.
Expired price.
Invalid UOM conversion.
Overlapping quantity tiers.
Duplicate RFQ conversion.
Insufficient supplier allocation.
Unavailable LLM.
Interrupted model download.
Web search failure.
Invalid supplier quotation document.
Database transaction failure.

All failures must be handled without corrupting approved data.

